\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\fs24 What is kubernetes?\line\b0 Kubernetes is container orchestration service its support docker image.It manage group of containers across multiple server or virtual machine and it is self-healing if any container crashed kubernetes will automatically restart or launch another new pods automatically.Kubernetes scales the application based on the workload and metric\line thereshold\par
Kubernetes componenets:\line Kubernetes cluster consists of master node and worker node\line\line Master node componenets:\line kube-apiserver\line kube-scheduler\line kube-controller-manager\line etcd\line\line Worker node components:\line Kubelet\line kube-proxy\line Container runtime\line\line\b Master node components:\line Kube-apiserver:\line\b0 Apiserver act as front end for the kubernetes control plane and it is used to receive request and send response to the worker node \par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b Kube-scheduler:\line\b0 Kube-scheduler takes responsabelities to launch newly created pods on running node\line\line\b Kube-controller-manager:\line\b0 Control plane component that runs controller processes\line\line\b Types of Controller:\line Node controller: \line\b0 Responsible for noticing and responding when nodes go down.\line\b Job controller\b0 : \line Watches for Job objects that represent one-off tasks, then creates Pods to run those tasks to completion.\line\b EndpointSlice controller\b0 : \line Populates EndpointSlice objects (to provide a link between Services and Pods).\line\b ServiceAccount controller\b0 : \line Create default ServiceAccounts for new namespaces.\line\line\b Worker node components:\line Kubelet:\line\b0 kubelet its an agent that runs on each node in the kubernetes cluster.It makes sure that containers are running in the pod and its ensure that the containers described in those PodSpecs are running and healthy.\line\line\b Kube-proxy\b0 :\line Kube-proxy is a network proxy that runs on each node in the kubernetes cluster its maintaining network rules on node this networks allows you to communicate to pods from network session inside or outside of the cluster\line\line\b Container runtime\b0 :\line Container runtime that empowers kubernetes to run container effectively.Its responsible for managing the execution and lifecycle of containers within the Kubernetes environment.\line\line\b Pods:\b0\line A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes. It runs one or more containers that share the same network and storage.\line A Pod gets an IP address, but the IP is usually temporary. If the Pod is deleted or recreated, its IP can change.\line\line\b Deployments:\line\b0 Deployment manages Pods for you. Instead of manually creating Pods, we normally create a Deployment and tell Kubernetes how many replicas we want.\par
\b Services\b0 :\line Service provides a stable network endpoint for accessing Pods.Pods can be recreated and their IP addresses can change, so applications should not directly depend on individual Pod IPs.\par
\b Namespaces\b0 :\line Namespace provides logical separation inside a Kubernetes cluster.It is useful for separating environments, teams, or applications.\line\b\line How they work together\line Namespace\b0 : organizes and separates resources.\par
\b Deployment\b0 : manages how many Pods should run and handles updates/replacements.\par
\b Pods\b0 : actually run the application containers.\par

